From 034aebaea24b5764d99c89e0b7922ef24c691e87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zahary Karadjov <zahary@agent-harbor.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:49:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] test(vm2): a shippable in-memory contract DB, and a
 checkpoint coordinator
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds simulation::MemoryContractDB in simulation/standalone/, beside the
PureContractDB decorator that needs a raw ContractDBInterface, and points the
avm.wasm reactor at it instead of TestContractDB from vm2/testing/.

The store is what the two existing in-memory copies are not. add_contracts is
implemented against the field layouts the TypeScript publishers define, so a
transaction that publishes a contract class and then calls into it works;
TestContractDB's add_contracts is a no-op and FuzzerContractDB's instance
decoder reads (tag, version, address) where upstream writes
(tag, address, version) and stops two public-key fields short.
get_debug_function_name answers from registered DebugFunctionNameHints —
upstream's own type, the one ExecutionHints already carries — rather than
returning nullopt unconditionally as both copies do. And committing or
reverting with no checkpoint open throws, with the TypeScript
PublicContractsDB's own two messages, instead of silently doing nothing.

Adds CheckpointCoordinator beside it: the single owner of the two independent
checkpoint stacks ContractDBInterface and LowLevelMerkleDBInterface each
declare. One create is one on each DB, the ContractDBInterface it hands out is
the PureContractDB decorator rather than the raw store, and it compares both
DBs' checkpoint ids against its own depth before and after every operation, so
a stack moved outside it is reported by name rather than surfacing later as a
root that cannot be explained.

Exports the coordinator and the contract DB's checkpoint id from the reactor
(49 exports, up from 39; the twelve imports are unchanged), and adds an
avm_differential contractdbinputs mode that prints what a host needs to drive
all of it, including deployment logs a Node script decodes with upstream's own
ContractClassPublishedEvent.fromLog and ContractInstancePublishedEvent.fromLog.

The reactor no longer links vm2/testing/ at all.
